ProsperoSunshine: a hook for each log record, and a call before each port is bound

The record hook lets the host decide what the log file gets in place of a record (src/log/log_filter.hpp): at debug
level print_req logs every query argument, including the stream's AES key (rikey from /launch) and the pairing
handshake, and nvhttp logs the client's certificate; the hook hides those values in every build, and the debug build
also masks addresses and holds back floods of similar lines. The hook may return no record, the record or several (a
summary first), so the sink no longer adds the newline: the formatter ends each line itself, and a record held back
leaves no empty line.

platf::trace_call runs right before the HTTP(S), RTSP and stream ports are bound. The debug build writes it to
host_diag.log, on disk before the call, so a host that hangs there shows which port it was binding.

